80:`agentTeam.enabled` exposes the root Session’s saved selection. New Sessions default to false; `team/mode` records explicit selections. Historical tasks imply enabled until an explicit selection. Only the root can call `setEnabled`; descendants share that mode. The Web menu calls the same method through `remote.agentTeams.setEnabled`, with the root Session id resolved to its live Agent by the Gateway. Mode writes take effect before awaiting persistence. Tools resolve availability at step preparation; prompt providers read the selection when evaluated. Task mutations check the current mode when their queued operation starts; admitted mutations may finish. Mode changes do not end inbox waits. A failed flush leaves the appended selection active; retrying the same selection flushes it without a duplicate event.

